   "fix": "Let the grid fill the canvas (columns in fr units), or centre a capped canvas with equal margins. A dead strip on one side reads as unfinished."
  },
  {
   "level": "WARN",
   "id": "heavy-borders",
   "width": 1440,
   "message": "50 panel borders are dark against their ground: #ffffff on #111318 (18.58:1) | #ffffff on #111318 (18.58:1) | #ffffff on #111318 (18.58:1)",
   "fix": "A panel border is a whisper: about 1.1–1.3:1 against its ground on a light screen (#e5e7eb–#ededed on white), and about 1.2–1.5:1 on a dark one (#1a1a1a on #000, #2e2e2e on #111). Darker lines turn the screen into a grid of boxes; keep the stronger line for controls.",
   "alsoAt": [
    768,
    390
   ]
  },
  {
   "level": "WARN",
   "id": "ragged-row",
   "width": 1440,
   "message": "2 pair(s) of cards in one row end at different heights (by 28px, 28px).",
   "fix": "Cards that share a row share a bottom edge: balance them by their content (the same number of rows, a block of similar height beside it), or stack them. In testing, ragged rows were marked down every time.",
